WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.710
Same defect. Another batch on hold.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.370
Did the last fix actually work?

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.790
Say your inspection team finds holes out
of tolerance again.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.320
In Improvements, record the
non-conformance and put the affected batch
on

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:20.240
hold. Use Five Whys to trace the problem
to a drill bit that stayed in

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.690
service too long because there was no tool
change limit.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.510
Assign someone to set that limit and give
them a due date.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:32.720
Then have a separate verifier check the
next three batches, and

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.350
record the results before closing the
action.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.620
If the defect comes back, your team can
see exactly what changed and what

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:46.540
was checked. Book a demo with ISO
Certification Consultants.
